# There are NO configuration environment variables.
#
# Everything — single sign-on, Uptime Kuma, session lifetime, the message of the
# day — is configured in the admin area and stored in the database, so it takes
# effect immediately and survives redeploys.
#
# The two variables below are the only exceptions, because they can't live in the
# database: you can't read the location of the database out of the database.
# Both have working defaults, so a normal deploy sets neither.

# DATABASE_PATH=/data/userportal.db
# UPLOADS_DIR=/data/uploads

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Legacy seeding (optional, first boot only)
#
# On a brand-new database these are read ONCE to pre-fill the corresponding
# settings, then never again. They exist only so an existing env-configured
# deployment carries over. Prefer configuring in the UI.
#
# KUMA_BASE_URL=
# KUMA_STATUS_SLUG=
# OIDC_ISSUER=
# OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# OIDC_DISPLAY_NAME=
